seg-12a295fba8a5 = Every capability in the verification matrix is labelled <b>validated</b> (checked against an independent external oracle), <b>modelled</b> or <b>partner-owned</b>; optical-clock figures are space goals on ground hardware (no strontium optical clock has flown). Maturity is <em>not</em> uniform across domains — Earth PNT is validated against real data; deep-space and Mars navigation is modelled, with only its building blocks (light time, planet positions) validated against external oracles; real-mission deep-space OD (orbit determination) is on the roadmap.

# text
# c1: kshana kinds
# c2: gnss-ssv
# c3: lunar-infrastructure
# c4: holdover-test
seg-3de57431d3e6 = The engine has { "87" } scenario kinds; <c1/> lists them with their fields. New in { "0.38.0" }: <c2/> (GNSS signals for spacecraft above, around and past the GNSS orbits) and <c3/> (lunar orbit and surface as navigation and geodetic infrastructure), both MODELLED, and <c4/> (a time-error record against the ITU-T masks).

# text
seg-68ed88ec0b32 = <b>Spectrum</b>: how a jammer takes the GNSS L band, band by band.

# text
seg-f04a0aeeee33 = <b>Clocks and timing</b>: holdover against a threshold, time transfer, and telecom holdover against the masks of the International Telecommunication Union's standardization sector (ITU-T).

# text
seg-7e38ac603ef2 = <b>Constellations around any body</b>: coverage, dilution of precision and availability around the Earth, the Moon or Mars, and the solar system at one epoch.

# text
seg-82708b06dcc6 = <b>Low-Earth-orbit navigation</b>: signal, pass and link, navigation message, and a fused fix, stage by stage.

# text
seg-e21e9bb02d00 = <b>Campaigns</b>: a chained mission, a sweep or a Monte Carlo ensemble in one scenario.

# text
seg-ba5057da54e4 = <b>Reports, animation and exports</b>: every figure with its unit and label; an animated drawing of a run; SP3 (Standard Product { "3" }), CCSDS (Consultative Committee for Space Data Systems) orbit messages, CZML (Cesium Language), KML (Keyhole Markup Language), GeoJSON, STK (Systems Tool Kit) and SigMF (Signal Metadata Format) files.

